      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The pressure at the common reference must be the same, for both the liquids. Since both tubes are open to the atmosphere, we must have</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>g</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>h</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>t</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>∝</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ρ</mi></mfrac></math></p>",
    "image": null
